From fb959de6049f351539b96514af302ce035690d18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:52:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] leantar: add batch packing (-p -) and --level

`-p -` packs many archives in one process from a JSON list on stdin,
in parallel, with each worker thread reusing its zstd contexts and the
dictionary prepared once per level. `--level N` sets the zstd level.
The archive format is unchanged, and single-archive packing without
--level runs the old code path byte for byte.

Each record is { out, trace, files?, base? }, like a single-archive
pack command. base is parsed as for -x -j (now shared in parse_base and
apply_base): a string or a list whose entry i overrides the i-th -C
directory, with null keeping it.

Compressors also builds without the zstd-dict feature (and without
zstd), where the olean path then uses the plain context.

